  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1103.08 Specifications and Dimensions for Designated Beaches or Flow-through Bathing Places",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1103.08 Specifications and Dimensions for Designated Beaches or Flow-through Bathing Places. The specifications required by Env-Wq 1103.02(c)(3) shall be as follows:\n\n(a) Measurements of:\n\n(1) Shore frontage of beach or access to flow-through bathing place, in feet;\n\n(2) Width of beach or access to flow-through bathing place, in feet; and\n\n(3) The surface area of the beach or access to flow-through bathing place, in square feet;\n\n(b) The maximum water depth, in feet, at the edge of the swimming area or at the float line;\n\n(c) The surface area of the swimming area, in square feet;\n\n(d) The maximum expected bather load and whether the beach or flow-through bathing place will have one or more lifeguards; and\n\n(e) Information on how construction of the beach or access to flow-through bathing place will comply with RSA 482-A, Dredge and Fill in Wetlands, and RSA 483-B, the Shoreland Water Qualify Protection Act.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) #8468, eff 11-1-05; ss by #10577, eff 5-1-14 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100); ss by #13198, eff 5-1-21 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100)",
